4. The Parallel Adaptive Institution

4.1 Architecture Overview

The Parallel Adaptive Institution (PAI) is a governance architecture designed for Regime B and Regime C conditions. Its purpose is not to match the speed of AI but to maintain stable coupling with it. Its design draws on the Viable System Model (Beer), dual control theory (Feldbaum; Wittenmark), and the adaptive governance literature (Folke; Olsson).

4.2 VSM Mapping

The institutional state vector:

I_t = (K_t, R_t, A_t, L_t, S_t) \tag{5}

where $K_t$ is institutional knowledge, $R_t$ is regulatory rules, $A_t$ is available capabilities, $L_t$ is legitimacy constraints, and $S_t$ is safety/societal state, maps onto VSM subsystems as follows:

