Reciprocal Recognition Protocol. A settlement's claim to self-governance is recognized when (a) quantitative thresholds are met and (b) a majority of other settlements in the same layer recognize the claim. Polycentric recognition, not central adjudication.

To prevent collusion, recognition criteria should incorporate Ostrom's design principles: clearly defined boundaries, congruence with local conditions, collective-choice arrangements, monitoring, graduated sanctions, conflict-resolution mechanisms, recognition of rights to organize, and nested enterprises.

Treaty compatibility: OST (1967), Liability Convention (1972), Registration Convention (1975). The PAI specifies implementation mechanisms where these are silent or contested; it does not supersede them.

